# With Textual's default ("RejoinChannelOnLocalKick" off), a KICK of
# ourselves leaves the channel parted and says nothing about rejoining. At
# the next connect a configured channel is joined again (performAutoJoin);
# one that is not configured stays parted.
= autojoin #c
! welcome
< :textual!u@h JOIN #c
> MODE #c
< :textual!u@h JOIN #d
> MODE #d
< :op!o@h KICK #c textual :bye
? line #c op kicked textual from the channel (bye)
? parted #c
? rejoin #c no
< :op!o@h KICK #d textual :bye
? line #d op kicked textual from the channel (bye)
? rejoin #d no
@ +10s
? lines #c 2
! closed eof
? notice Disconnected: the server closed the connection; reconnecting in 5 s
! connect
> dial #2 irc.test:6667 plain
? notice Connecting to irc.test:6667
! opened
> CAP LS 302
> NICK textual
> USER textual 0 * Textual
< :irc.test 001 textual :Welcome
> JOIN #c
? parted #d
? rejoin #d no
? registered textual
